(window.StoryDialogue = window.StoryDialogue || {})["ac-12"] = {"468369101":[["","Hey, hey, you should be able to hear me, right!? Time is limited, so I'll keep it short!"],["","Vincenza, watch out for Carlo!"],["","He suddenly attacked my team with his men—zzzzt—trying to take the box Genovese gave me!"],["","If I'm right, his real target has to be—zzzt—"],["","Wh—zzzt—interference—I've got to—"],["","—run—"],["Contactor Gerard","Where's my cargo?"],["Luno Family Member","In the truck. I'll take you over so you can check it."],["Contactor Gerard","Don't bother. I know how you guys operate, and I'm not looking to play games here... Here's the rest of what I owe."],["Contactor Gerard","Pleasure doing business."],["","The contact, Gerard, sets down the briefcase and immediately gets to his feet, clearly unwilling to stay a second longer."],["Luno Family Member","Wait, there's one more thing... we're looking for someone."],["","As he's handed the photo, Gerard's brow tightens almost instinctively."],["Luno Family Member","Bertha Wagner, do you know where she went?"],["Contactor Gerard","No, I haven't seen her."],["Luno Family Member","That so? As far as I know, she was here three days ago and made contact with a handler named Gerard—a fact the bartender backed up."],["Luno Family Member","If you can't remember, I can help you recall..."],["","The Luno Family members across the table also stand up and walk over."],["Contactor Gerard","...Damn it!"],["","Gerard suddenly takes off running, but his path is blocked by several figures that appear out of nowhere."],["","Don't be in such a hurry to leave, Mr. Gerard."],["","Get out of my way!"],["","Steeling himself, he reaches for the detonator hidden at his waist—"],["","XC 119, a March afternoon, Southeast District of Burton Bay..."],["","About two kilometers from the docks, there's an old bar at a crossroads. Its name is absurdly long and complicated, so no one ever remembers it—everyone just calls it \"the Bar.\""],["","With music drifting out from within, the bartender, who also doubles as the doorman, slumps in his chair, head bobbing unevenly as if he might fall asleep at any moment."],["","Not surprising. It's a weekday afternoon, around three, with most regulars still down at the docks and anyone passing through just grabbing a drink and leaving."],["","If there's anything unusual, it's the two attractive women who walked in an hour ago. He has no idea what their story is, or if he'll ever get the chance to find out."],["","Bang—!!"],["Bartender","Wh-What the hell was that?!"],["","A sudden blast and a blinding flash of white rip through the shop, snapping the bartender wide awake."],["","Then comes a burst of gunfire, mixed with the crash of overturned tables and shattering glass. A figure staggers out, blood pouring from his shoulder."],["Contactor Gerard","Damn that crazy woman, even after eating a flashbang, she still managed to hit me...!"],["","Grimacing through the pain, he pulls out his communicator and sends out an emergency call as fast as he can."],["Contactor Gerard","My cover's blown—spring the trap!"],["Bartender","What happened? You've been shot—"],["Contactor Gerard","Move!"],["","Gerard shoves the bartender aside without hesitation and rushes straight toward a nearby garage."],["","Unlocking the door, he yanks back the curtain. The ST is already prepped, half-kneeling on the deck—once he hits the cockpit, he can strike back."],["","Hide-and-seek's over, Mr. Gerard."],["","A cold, unnatural chill creeps up the back of his neck, forcing him to freeze mid-motion."],["Contactor Gerard","...What do you want?"],["","Bertha Wagner's whereabouts and the full details of your recent dealings with the Luno Family. We need precise, accurate intel."],["","I told you, I don't know any damn Bertha!"],["","Don't bother asking me about those deals—you're the ones who ran them. Don't you know your own business—"],["","Mid-sentence, he suddenly realizes something is off."],["Contactor Gerard","Wait, you're not with Carlo?!"],["","A rush of hurried footsteps closes in. Gerard turns to see the woman who confronted him in the bar stumbling after him, anger written all over her face."],["Deborah","Watch it, Verna! She rigged a flashbang in her briefcase and took down half our people... Who knows what other tricks she's got up her sleeve!"],["Contactor Gerard","Did you say Vincenza?"],["","For a moment, Gerard forgets the danger. He forces his head to turn just enough to catch a glimpse of the person behind him, her refined features unmistakable. He doesn't know much about the Luno Family, but that face... there's no way he could get it wrong."],["Contactor Gerard","Vincenza Luno... It's you!"],["Contactor Gerard","Attacking the Harpy depot and colluding with the Ovett Revolutionary Army, was it all your idea? It seems the Luno Family has completely fallen!"],["Vincenza","...What?"],["","Vincenza frowns; nothing Gerard has said or done so far matches what they planned for."],["","He definitely mentioned Carlo. That's the exact family executive Vincenza is tracking—suspected of defying orders to smuggle heavy arms, and a key link to Bertha's disappearance."],["","But an attack on Harpy's depot? Working with the Ovett Revolutionary Army? That's the first she's heard of any of it."],["Vincenza","Looks like we need to have a proper talk, Gerard—"],["","A different possibility suddenly flashes through her mind."],["Vincenza","No... You're not the real Gerard, are you?"],["Vincenza","You didn't see through our cover, yet you rigged a flashbang trap. And the way you treated Ovett isn't how an informant talks to his contact... Who exactly are you?"],["Contactor Gerard","Heh. You'll find out, once you're in our interrogation room."],["","As if on cue, the communicators on Vincenza and Deborah suddenly blare with alarms."],["Luno Family Member","Boss, we've got heavy ST signatures in the area—they're heading right for you!"],["Deborah","Damn it, I've got visual confirmation too! Where the hell did they come from?!"],["Contactor Gerard","Things didn't go quite as planned, but you're not walking out of here—ghh—agh—?!"],["","A surge of current runs through his neck, precisely targeting the vagus nerve. Gerard lets out a strangled cry before losing consciousness and collapsing within seconds."],["","Casually tossing the stun gun aside, Vincenza walks away without looking back."],["Vincenza","Send a few people and keep an eye on him."],["Deborah","There are quite a few enemy units, and they're well-armed. What do you plan to do?"],["Vincenza","No matter who is behind this fake informant, we must keep the initiative in our hands."],["Vincenza","Power up the STs. Let's go win our leverage on the battlefield."],["","Shortly after the two leave, the comms unit beside the unconscious \"Gerard\" flickers to life."],["Gregory","Doug, we've completed the encirclement. What's your status?"],["Gregory","Doug? Answer me, what's going on?!"],["Gregory","...Damn that Luno Family!"],["Gregory","All units, advance! We need Carlo alive, and find Doug!"]],"468369301":[["","Despite their clear numerical advantage, the attacking ST force fails to break through the Luno Family's defenses."],["","With Vincenza acting as both command and firepower core, Luno's ST units use buildings and trees to stay in constant motion—spreading out, regrouping, and repeatedly tearing at the encirclement."],["Gregory","Since when did Carlo's legion have such tactical skills? They're like a real army..."],["","Gregory sensed something unusual shortly after the battle began."],["","As a fixer who's spent years hustling on Milkhama Island playing both sides of the law, he figures he knows how mafia families work well enough."],["","Loyal, reckless, aggressive... the last thing they should look like is this cold and calculated, the Carlo Legion under the Luno Family included."],["","But these enemies are different. The STs bear the Luno Family emblem, yet every maneuver screams professional discipline—just like the UNCS agents Gregory once dealt with."],["Gregory","...Damn it! Everyone, cease fire!"],["","Gregory's ST fires multiple green and white signal flares into the air while simultaneously switching communications to the public channel."],["Gregory","Hold your fire, both sides! There's been some kind of mistake—stand down!"],["Gregory","I'm Gregory Gannibal, acting under commission from the Harpy Guild! I'm here to investigate the attack on the arms depot by Carlo's forces!"],["Gregory","Hold your fire and state your callsign! Let's put an end to this farce!"],["","Gregory walks his ST out into the open alone, stomach churning. If he's wrong about this, or if the other side just doesn't play by the rules, his life becomes the cheapest, most pathetic gamble he's ever made."],["Vincenza","The Harpy Guild, huh? Since when did you become the police of Milkhama?"],["","As the communication window comes into view, Gregory gasps."],["Gregory","What...? Vincenza Luno?!"],["Gregory","So that's what happened! What a huge misunderstanding!"],["","After confirming identities, the battle quickly ceases. The injured are settled, and the belated UNCS officers are sent away. Finally, representatives from both sides leave their STs to exchange information face to face."],["Gregory","So the trade intel we leaked while posing as informants ended up in your hands? I was sure it would be Carlo's people showing up."],["Deborah","That was supposed to be our line. We deliberately had someone pose as Carlo's crew for the deal, and instead we ran straight into Harpy."],["Deborah","If Vincenza hadn't held back our firepower during the engagement, who knows how many people would've died for nothing."],["","Gregory stiffens slightly. He knows he didn't gain the upper hand in the fight, but he never expected they'd been showing restraint the whole time."],["","A different kind of unease creeps in... he can feel himself losing the initiative in this negotiation."],["","Sensing the moment, Vincenza turns the pressure onto him."],["Vincenza","Gregory Gannibal. Judging by your name, appearance, and accent, you're Ovettian. How does a man like you come into the service of Harpy?"],["Gregory","...That's right. I am from the Principality of Ovett. But don't get the wrong idea, not every Ovettian wants to stir up trouble in Milkhama."],["Gregory","I'm just a trader, moving between the island and the mainland, making enough to get by. I have some ties with a regional agent from Harpy, so I was asked to look into the attack on the arms depot by Carlo's forces and the theft of those weapons."],["Gregory","I didn't expect Miss Vincenza to be investigating this personally as well."],["","Though a smile sits on his face, Gregory's eyes stay locked on Vincenza. He needs to read her intent: As the current head of the family, where does Vincenza Luno truly stand when it comes to Carlo?"],["Gregory","Now that the misunderstanding's cleared, we won't interfere with your operation. That said, Miss Vincenza, I'd appreciate any intel you can share, so I have something to report back to Harpy..."],["Vincenza","Of course. Since we're both after Carlo Kottel, it only makes sense to exchange what we know."],["Vincenza","Deborah."],["","Catching the cue, Deborah turns and waves her men over, who drag in a gaunt man with a burlap sack over his head."],["Gregory","...And this is?"],["Vincenza","Savage—Carlo's trusted man, and the handler for this shipment. He's yours now."],["","The casual tone nearly brings Gregory out in a cold sweat. He knows it's a squeeze—he has to produce equal leverage, and fast."],["","At the same time, he realizes something else. Vincenza has no intention of covering for Carlo. If anything, she's preparing to strike hard."],["Gregory","Your methods are... impressive, Miss Vincenza. In that case, I suppose I should show some sincerity as well."],["","He reaches into his coat, pulls out a notebook packed with tabs, and hands it over."],["Gregory","These are the results of our investigation so far. I've also included the fragments of intel provided by the real contact, Gerard."],["Gregory","You probably know Carlo's outfit better than I do anyway. So I'll keep it simple and stick to the ones they're dealing with—the Muskrat Mercenaries."],["Gregory","This mercenary group is largely made up of an Ovett Revolutionary Army advance team. Harpy has had them under surveillance for quite some time. They used to operate near the Central Mines, but recently they've resurfaced near Kadrey without a trace."],["Vincenza","Carlo maintains the transit corridor between the Central Mines and Kadrey. He has the means to move personnel and materiel off the books."],["Gregory","Caught flat-footed, the Harpy depot on the outskirts of Kadrey didn't even have time to sound the alarm before the Muskrats and Carlo's outfit made off with a massive stash of arms and supplies."],["Deborah","No wonder the Carlo Legion has grown so rapidly... Vincenza, you'd better prepare for the worst."],["Vincenza","Got it."],["","For the first time, a hint of gravity settles over Vincenza's striking features. Internal rebellion, combined with infiltration by the Ovett Revolutionary Army—either alone would be dangerous. Together, they're enough to shake the very foundation of the Luno Family's survival."],["","She leafs through the notebook, checking Gregory's notes against her own intel... until a photo tucked between the pages catches her eye."],["","The photo is a grainy, long-range shot—just two figures barely recognizable as they climb into an armored vehicle."],["","However, one figure's clothing, hair, and even the weapon in their hand are splashed with flamboyant colors that Vincenza knows well."],["Vincenza","Bertha...? When was this photo taken?"],["Gregory","This? About three days ago, taken by our people when the Muskrat Mercenaries were relocating... Recognize anyone?"],["","Thinking about what this means for Bertha, Vincenza hesitates."],["","Bertha's earlier warning said Carlo's outfit was right on her tail, yet here she is in the photo, moving alongside the Muskrats... Did she flip, or is there more to this?"],["Vincenza","We need to find these Muskrat Mercenaries as soon as possible."],["Gregory","Well, I hope so too, but they're scattered, always on the move. We still haven't located their base. Even Gerard, their contact, has to wait for the higher-ups to call and let him know where the cargo's headed."],["Gregory","We were hoping that setting up this trap would catch Carlo's men and lead us to some useful intel, but it seems we've come up empty-handed."],["Vincenza","Empty-handed? Quite the opposite, Gregory. This meeting has convinced me that we've pieced together a powerful hand."],["Gregory","Meaning?"],["Vincenza","Between the two of us, we've got the contacts for both Carlo and the Muskrats. So why not turn up the heat on this little show...?"],["Vincenza","\"We detected Vincenza Luno tailing the drop, jumped her, and took her captive. Awaiting further instructions\"..."],["Vincenza","Use this setup to bait those self-righteous idiots into taking the hook."]],"468373101":[["Harpy Contact","As you asked, I've spread the word that the Luno Family clashed with some unknown force near Burton Bay."],["Harpy Contact","But so far, aside from a few reckless unaffiliated mercs, no one with real backing has come sniffing around for intel."],["Gregory","As long as it looks believable, that's enough. It's just to give this act some weight... Anyway, thanks. I'll contact you if anything changes."],["","After ending the call, Gregory looks over at Vincenza, who's sitting nearby, casually playing with a deck of cards."],["Gregory","So far, everything's gone according to plan. But honestly... I'm not convinced the other side will take the bait."],["Vincenza","The Muskrats might be cautious and see zero value in me, but not Carlo; he'd never miss an opportunity to put me in the ground."],["Gregory","...Could you elaborate?"],["","Vincenza doesn't answer directly. She simply gestures toward the seat across from her—an invitation."],["","With no urgent matters at hand, Gregory yields to her wishes, pulls up a chair, and sits down."],["Vincenza","Carlo has always opposed my taking over as head of the Luno Family. He's defied my orders more than once. From what I've heard, he's even been telling his own people that I'm the one who's tearing the family apart."],["","As she speaks, Vincenza signals a nearby Luno member to bring over two cocktails. Gregory doesn't hesitate. He picks one up and downs half in a single go."],["Gregory","Damn good drink. If I'm not mistaken, that's a gin fizz—heavy on the lime, touch of simple syrup, topped with soda."],["Gregory","Bit weak for an Ovett guy like me, though."],["","Turning the glass in his hand, Gregory gathers his thoughts."],["Gregory","Genovese Luno... has he weighed in on Carlo going rogue?"],["Vincenza","The Legion answers to the family, and only to the head. And by the same rule, dealing with a rogue subordinate is the head's responsibility—that's always been the way."],["Gregory","An eagle lets its young fall off a cliff so they learn to fly... I see. Guess that was a stupid question."],["","Before the words fully settle, the communicator on the table starts to buzz."],["Harpy Contact","Gregory, the fish took the bait—we've just received intel. Carlo Legion forces are moving from the eastern side of Kadrey toward Burton Bay!"],["Harpy Contact","Exact numbers are unclear, but at least two ST companies along with armed vehicles. You'd better be ready!"],["Gregory","...That was fast. Looks like they're really set on you."],["","Draining the rest of his drink, Gregory relays combat readiness orders through his communicator to the units lying in wait."],["Gregory","I'll have to excuse myself for now, Miss Vincenza. I still need to finish setting the stage."],["Vincenza","I understand. I'll remain here and play the hostage until the main act begins... I look forward to your good news."],["","The perimeter of the meeting point is unprecedentedly lively—nearly ten STs painted with the Luno Family emblem arrive first, forming a circle about fifty meters from the store and closing off the roads on both sides."],["","Several sedans and armed pickups then park separately. Dozens of Legion members get out of the vehicles, weapons in hand, completely surrounding the street."],["","Doug—the Harpy operative who had the bad luck of catching a bullet while posing as Gerard the contact—is still playing his part with bandaged wounds, waiting by the door to welcome Carlo."],["Doug","Gregory... this doesn't look good."],["","The Carlo Legion is advancing in force, their scale of armament far beyond expectations. Doug can only lower his voice, quietly voicing his concern to Gregory beside him."],["Doug","If these lunatics make a move directly, our people won't be able to stop them in time."],["Gregory","Whether they make a move depends on how well we play our roles."],["Doug","Stop putting on the pressure, man. My legs are starting to shake, and the gunshot wound on my shoulder seems to be getting more painful... ah."],["","Doug cuts off mid-complaint. Gregory follows his eyes: a man in a sharp suit approaches, flanked by bodyguards."],["Gregory","Carlo Kottel's here... Let's go. Time to heat things up."],["","Gregory puts on a bright smile and goes up to greet him with Doug."],["Gregory","Oh my—Mr. Carlo himself, what an honor. My apologies for not greeting you sooner."],["","A bodyguard blocks the way, warning Gregory with a fierce look not to approach."],["Gregory","Ah—my mistake! Let me introduce myself! I'm Bekov of the Muskrat Mercenaries, and this here is Gerard, who's done business with your Legion before."],["","Carlo barely spares him a glance before frowning, clearly annoyed."],["Carlo","Tsk, another Ovettian... Enough talking. Where is Vincenza Luno?"],["Gregory","She's being held in the innermost room. Dangerous woman, took out quite a few of our people. Your man Savage was injured and knocked out as well. He's being treated in the main hall."],["","As he speaks, Gregory hands over a communication terminal. The building's internal surveillance feed is displayed on the screen."],["","After a brief glance at Savage, his unconscious lieutenant, Carlo turns all his attention to the feed from the locked room—Vincenza is tied to a chair, looking battered and disheveled, two armed guards standing over her."],["","Carlo signals his men to verify the situation, and within moments, they confirm the footage is genuine."],["Carlo","Hahahaha!"],["Carlo","I knew this day was coming for you, Vincenza Luno!"],["","Carlo bursts into unrestrained laughter and tosses the terminal back to Gregory."],["Carlo","You've done well! So, what do the Muskrat Mercenaries want?"],["Carlo","More weapons? Or maybe more informants planted in Laplace and Kadrey?"],["Gregory","Well... we're just the ones carrying out orders..."],["Carlo","Hmph, fair enough. Then bring Andrea here. I'll deal with her personally."],["","Andrea. Hearing that name, it takes all Gregory has to keep from reacting."],["","This name has appeared several times in Harpy's intel, but the incidents tied to it never seemed connected, so the intel officers came to believe she was just an ordinary mercenary working for money."],["Gregory","We've already reached out to our leader, but she's tied up with another urgent operation... How about this—we'll leave the person inside to you, Mr. Carlo."],["Gregory","As for future cooperation between the Muskrat Mercenaries and the Carlo Legion, our leader can discuss it with you once she returns. Given our history and your reputation, I'm sure you won't go back on your word."],["Carlo","You've got a good head on your shoulders, Bekov. I'll admit, I underestimated you at first. Fine, we'll do it your way. As a down payment, this batch is yours."],["","Carlo casually gestures toward the armed pickups behind him. The cargo beds are stacked with various standard-issue firearms."],["Carlo","Straight out of UNCS stock. If you're planning anything in Sankara or with the Dawnstar League, these will come in handy."],["Gregory","Ah, you're too kind. Looks like we picked the right partners after all—I'll have her brought out immediately..."],["Carlo","Wait. Just have your people and Savage come out. Leave Vincenza Luno inside."],["Gregory","You mean...?"],["Carlo","Taking Vincenza away will only attract the GSA. I need her dead here, leaving no trace—flatten the building, and leave no debris behind!"],["","In about five minutes, everyone inside clears out, leaving only Vincenza tied to her chair on the feed—she seems to sense something, twisting against the ropes."],["","Carlo holds a cigarette between his lips. A storm of conflicting emotions flickers across his face, settling into cold murderous intent."],["Carlo","Leave the future of the family to me, Vincenza Luno."],["","He raises a hand, and the Carlo Legion STs bring their weapons up, training them on the building."],["","But before Carlo drops his hand, a blast rocks the compound."],["Carlo","What!?"],["","The building stands untouched; instead, a Carlo Legion ST collapses, spitting sparks and electrical flash."],["Carlo's Subordinate","Boss, i-it's an attack!! We've been locked by the radar—ugh!!"],["","With almost no time to react, the STs of the Carlo Legion are attacked one after another, erupting where they stand."],["Carlo","...Bekov, you bastard!"],["","A split second too late, Carlo realizes it's a trap. He flies into a rage and opens fire, but Gregory and Doug are ready for it, diving for cover behind the vehicles the moment he moves."],["","Almost simultaneously, a smoke grenade arcs down, billowing out to blanket the ground around Carlo—blinding the Legion members and cloaking Gregory's team."],["Carlo","Groups one and two, find those two bastards! The rest of you, come with me, quickly!!"],["","Rat-tat-tat—automatic fire chatters. Carlo Legion reinforcements scrambling to back him up don't even make it into the smoke before a hail of lead drops them one by one."],["Carlo","Damn it, everyone, protect me!!!"],["","Under the cover of smoke, Carlo can barely see the positions of his subordinates and can only move aimlessly toward the barely visible STs on his side."],["","Just as he is about to break clear of the smoke, a black barrel jabs out from the haze, pressing hard against his skull."],["Gregory","This is game over."],["Carlo","Who are you?! Who the hell are you?!"],["Gregory","Gregory Gannibal, Harpy Guild. You're coming with us, Mr. Carlo Kottel—"],["Doug","Watch out, enemy incoming!"],["","A streak of silver flashes out from the smoke. Even with Doug's warning, Gregory barely twists out of the way. The razor edge slices through his clothes, carving a nasty gash along his arm."],["","By the time he plants his feet, a man in a suit and a black cowboy hat is already standing by Carlo's side."],["Carlo","Cough, cough... Garcia, what took you so long!"],["Garcia","I warned you Vincenza Luno wasn't an easy mark, but you insisted on showing up in person."],["Garcia","Now come. Get in the ST and let's get out of here."],["","Garcia spares Gregory only a passing glance before escorting Carlo back into the smoke. Moments later, a handful of shouting Carlo Legion grunts close in."],["Gregory","We've been outmaneuvered. I didn't expect Carlo to have helpers."],["Doug","Boss, what should we do?"],["Gregory","...Pull back. Staying here will only get in our allies' way."],["","Gregory heads for the safe zone, pulling out a small communicator that's still active."],["Gregory","You heard everything, didn't you, Miss Vincenza?"],["Vincenza","I heard everything—your talk with Carlo, and... Garcia crashing the party."],["","The moment he breaks through the smoke, Gregory clearly sees allied forces punching through the Carlo Legion's blockade, bringing a heavily armored ST equipped with a shoulder-mounted rail gun up near the building."],["Vincenza","Harpy will prioritize your extraction. From here on out, this is Luno Family business."]],"468373301":[["","After nearly an hour of fighting, the battle is over."],["","Cratered ruins, mangled STs, and bodies torn beyond recognition... The grounds once set aside for Burton Bay dockworkers to unwind have turned into complete hell."],["","Even with Garcia's reinforcements stabilizing the line for a time, the Carlo Legion is ultimately outmatched by Vincenza's forces."],["","Yet instead of pressing the attack, her side holds back. Only Vincenza steps forward, piloting a towering ST on her own."],["Vincenza","I ran through every possibility... and you still weren't one of them."],["Carlo","Then stop talking and finish it!"],["Vincenza","I'm not talking to you, Carlo Kottel."],["","Her Colossus trains its rail gun straight at Carlo's battered ST. If she wants, a high-caliber slug will punch through the cockpit in the next second."],["Carlo","You b—"],["Garcia","Stop provoking her."],["","Garcia pilots his ST forward to meet the Colossus head-on."],["Garcia","...What do you want to say, Vincenza?"],["Vincenza","Tell me, Garcia, why are you siding with Carlo? Is it because of your mother?"],["Garcia","...Yes, but not entirely. The Carlo Legion helped me with the drug supply issue, but that's not the only reason."],["","On the comms channel, facing the new leader he once swore to protect, Garcia wears a conflicted expression."],["Garcia","Boss Luno said, \"The era of loyalty and brotherhood is over.\" I didn't get what he meant back then, but now I think I do."],["Garcia","You've done well, Vincenza, so well that you've almost changed the entire Luno Family in just a month."],["Garcia","Things that once took blood and vows to earn, now all you have to do is wag your tail for the GSA, and they're handed to you."],["Vincenza","Do you think like Carlo—that I'd sell out the family to Rosemary Jean?"],["Garcia","I trust you wouldn't, but the outcome won't hinge on your attitude, Vincenza. We've run over twenty ops with the GSA this past month alone; the sheer gap between both sides is obvious."],["Garcia","All it takes is a single thought from the Madam, and the ship carrying us will sink... The new era's sea will soon drown all of us."],["Garcia","No, even if Madam makes no move, vultures eyeing Port Kadrey like the Doll Group won't ever pass up a chance to kick us while we're down..."],["Vincenza","Afraid of change, so you waste your life on a place like this? I have to say, in all the time I've known you, this is easily the stupidest thing you've ever done."],["Garcia","I admit it. But this way, at least our lives stay in our own hands, instead of getting tossed into the fire as the GSA's dirty gloves one day, without even a scrap left behind."],["Vincenza","Looks like you really are stuck in the past... Unfortunately, I'm not about to play along with this outdated gamble."],["","The Colossus ST retracts its rail gun and moves aside to clear the way."],["Vincenza","...Go."],["","At Vincenza's signal, the encircling STs also make an opening."],["Garcia","...If it were your father, he would never let a traitor leave alive, even if it meant mutual destruction."],["Vincenza","Is that so? Personally, I think the man he is today would make the exact same call. And besides—"],["","A brief pause, and Vincenza makes her declaration, deadly serious and absolute."],["Vincenza","I am the current leader of the Luno Family, and your lives and deaths are determined by me."],["Vincenza","I will lead the family into a new era. Who should follow and who will fall behind, no one is qualified to judge except me, not even the GSA."],["","Garcia parts his lips, words failing him. A sudden daze washes over him as the striking woman before him blurs, snapping into place with the sharp, commanding silhouette etched into his memory."],["Garcia","...Heh, the power of bloodline is truly astonishing."],["Garcia","...I just hope you can actually pull it off."],["","With that, Garcia steers his ST toward the edge of the encirclement, and Carlo quickly follows. The Harpy operatives nearby exchange uncertain glances, unsure whether they should move to stop them."],["","Gregory emerges from out of nowhere, his arm wound already patched up. Watching Carlo and the others pull further away, he asks the burning question on Harpy's mind."],["Gregory","You're not really planning to just let them go, are you?"],["Vincenza","Of course not."],["","To Gregory's surprise, Vincenza responds without the slightest hesitation."],["","She switches comms channels and issues an order to a partner—one who has been on standby for a long time."],["Vincenza","Follow them, Deborah, and find their base."],["","Late that night, in a warehouse east of the United City of Laplace, Carlo is throwing a furious fit."],["Carlo","We lost a total of three squads!"],["Carlo","Just because you bastards didn't notice Gerard got swapped out, every damn ST, weapon, and soldier I had is gone!"],["","Unable to endure the accusation, the woman sitting across from him suddenly stands up, returning his look with cold eyes."],["Andrea","Watch your attitude, Mr. Carlo. The Muskrat Mercenaries are not your vassals, nor do we need to pay for your foolishness!"],["Andrea","If you had been willing to verify Savage's situation or wait for us to confirm the intel before taking action, you wouldn't have lost so disastrously today."],["Carlo","Just a pack of Ovett strays—!"],["","The nearly deranged Carlo attempts to draw his weapon, but Andrea moves much faster, pressing a pistol to his forehead."],["Garcia","Captain Andrea!"],["","Garcia can't tell what the Ovett mercenary will do, so he keeps his sights locked onto her and barks a warning. Taking the cue, fighters from both the Muskrat Mercenaries and Carlo's corps raise their weapons, leveling guns right back at each other."],["Andrea","Relax, I'm not like him. I'm not about to lose my head over some petty provocation."],["","Andrea disarms Carlo with a hard, practiced motion, then holsters her gun."],["Andrea","The most important thing now is to discuss our next plan of action."],["Garcia","...That's right. Vincenza is already aware of our cooperation. It's only a matter of time before she retaliates."],["","Knowing there's no point pushing it, Carlo kicks a nearby chair across the room, then turns the rest of his anger on people who aren't even in the room."],["Carlo","A counterattack? With what? A third of the family is already on our side!"],["Carlo","Even if she tries to buy off the fence-sitters, she's gotta bring enough to the table—and there's no way in hell she matches what we're holding!"],["Carlo","Move now, and Vincenza Luno and that ragtag Harpy crew won't even make a ripple!"],["Andrea","If that's your call, then the Muskrat Mercenaries won't argue."],["","Andrea knows Carlo's judgment is running on pure rage and humiliation, but she has no intention of stopping him. If anything, she's more than happy to fan the flames."],["","She takes out an ebony box from her coat, its surface adorned with the Luno family emblem."],["Andrea","Besides, this thing should help you clear some trouble."],["Carlo","That's Genovese's...! Why didn't you bring it out sooner!?"],["","Carlo snatches the box, his eyes burning with a feverish intensity, as if the anger from moments ago had never existed."],["Andrea","Don't underestimate Bertha. We spent quite a bit of effort to dig up the whereabouts of this thing from her."],["Andrea","According to the agreement, it now officially belongs to you."],["","Carlo opens the box and repeatedly checks its contents, even starting to smile."],["Carlo","With this, our odds at least double... No, Kadrey will truly be ours! Even the Doll Group will have to answer to us!"],["Carlo","Andrea, put your people behind this operation. When the dust settles, every shipment you're looking to run will have a clear route—guaranteed!"],["Andrea","It's a deal, Mr. Carlo."],["","Carlo and Andrea are instantly on the same page, leaving Garcia frowning on the sidelines."],["Garcia","..."],["","But he ultimately remains silent."]],"468377101":[["","Early the next morning—a nondescript house along the road from Kadrey toward Saget..."],["","From the outside, it looks like an ordinary logistics warehouse, but inside it's been converted into a fully functional base—this is the main stronghold of the Muskrat Mercenaries."],["","Andrea heads straight back here after wrapping up talks with the Carlo family, then makes her way to the back room serving as a makeshift cell."],["","Huff... huff... huh, try saying that again..."],["","I am... the future... legendary merc... huff..."],["","Opening the door, Andrea sighs; sprawled across the table ahead of her, a girl murmurs in her sleep."],["","Andrea clenches her fist and pounds on the door."],["Bertha","...Whoa! Wh-What's that sound?!"],["","The girl lying down suddenly awakens, looking nervously towards the door."],["Andrea","It's amazing you can sleep so soundly in this situation."],["Bertha","Oh, it's just Andrea... Next time you wake someone up, don't make such a scary noise."],["","Any tension instantly vanishes. Bertha goes to slump back over the table, only to freeze when she spots the puddle of drool she left behind from her awkward sleeping posture."],["","Seeing this, Andrea sighs again and hands over a tissue, which Bertha grabs. She pulls out a few sheets and wipes casually, then sits up straight, pretending nothing happened."],["Bertha","Cough... So, why are you here?"],["Bertha","You've taken all the boxes, so there shouldn't be anything you need from me, right?"],["Andrea","I have a proposal for you."],["","Short on time, Andrea skips the runaround and lays her cards on the table."],["Andrea","Bertha, join the Muskrat Mercenaries."],["Bertha","...Huh? Wait, what do you mean?"],["Andrea","The Carlo Legion will soon launch a surprise attack on Kadrey, and we will also deploy troops to assist in the battle."],["Andrea","Carlo Kottel will become the new head of the Luno Family. He's not a forgiving man. If you remain with the family, you'll be dealt with."],["Andrea","Seeing as we used to be comrades... you can join the Muskrat Mercenaries, ride out with me, and save your skin and your standing."],["","Bertha just stares at Andrea, as if trying to read something from her face. Andrea meets her eyes directly, waiting for her response."],["Bertha","What if I refuse?"],["Andrea","If not, then I will hand you over to the Carlo Legion according to the agreement."],["Bertha","......"],["Andrea","As a mercenary, you understand which choice serves your best interests, and you know I have no reason to deceive you on this."],["","Just as Andrea said, Bertha's life as a mercenary hasn't been smooth, but she's far from being an inexperienced rookie."],["","She knows the terms Andrea offers aren't bad, but—"],["Bertha","Andrea... my dream—do you remember?"],["Andrea","...I do. Being the strongest legendary merc. You brought it up at least twenty times a day back when we first teamed up."],["Bertha","Not that many, maybe seven or eight times... Ahem, that's not the point!"],["Bertha","What I want to say is, a legendary merc wouldn't abandon a commission just because they're afraid of dying."],["Bertha","Uncle Genovese entrusted the box to me because he believes I can keep it safe."],["Andrea","But the box has already fallen into Carlo's hands. Your commission has failed."],["Bertha","That's easy—I'll just find an opportunity to take it back! Besides..."],["Bertha","You used to be my subordinate, and now I have to call you captain... Honestly, it's a bit hard to swallow."],["","Andrea realizes then that she has misjudged Bertha. That girl who lost again and again, treating \"bouncing back\" like second nature, has begun to change."],["","Now she is no longer a qualified merc, looking more like a child driven by naive ideals, totally blind to the reality around her."],["Andrea","...Looks like the negotiation's over."],["","Andrea seems to lose interest and stops trying to persuade her, turning to walk out."],["Andrea","Stay here and wait for the battle to end."],["Bertha","Don't keep me waiting too long. It gets quite boring being alone."],["Bertha","And... thanks for the tissue."],["","Watching Bertha casually wave the tissue in her hand, Andrea lets out one last sigh before closing the door."],["","Another ten minutes pass in silence. Only after Andrea is long gone does Bertha finally stand up, pulling out the small lockpicking tool she has been hiding beneath her."],["Bertha","That was close... Good thing she didn't catch on..."],["","She moves quietly to the door, careful not to make a sound. After confirming there's only one half-asleep guard outside, she starts working the lock."],["Bertha","Sorry, Andrea... I was never planning to just sit here and wait."],["Muskrat Mercenary Captain","First team, head out as soon as you're done with preparations. Second team, go to Area C to reload. Third team, head to Area D—what, the machines aren't working? Then switch to Area B, quickly!"],["","Inside the Muskrat Mercenary stronghold, fighters of the Ovett Revolutionary Army run through their final pre-battle maintenance and line up in formation."],["","The tempo of recent operations has run them ragged and set back maintenance, yet they have to gear up on the double to sync with the Carlo Legion."],["","All the rush makes them careless, oblivious to the shadow already slipping deep inside the base."],["Deborah","At least four combat-ready ST squads in this base alone. Guess the Muskrats aren't small-time after all."],["Deborah","Chances are, even Carlo had no idea his partner was holding this many cards in reserve."],["","She records the vital intel, planting timed charges in the shadows along the way."],["","Just then, an alarm suddenly blares. Deborah stops immediately, rolling behind a container as she cautiously observes the enemy's movements."],["Deborah","...No, something's wrong. The alarm wasn't triggered here. Their target is—"],["Bertha","Aaaaargh! Who the hell puts an alarm in the kitchen?! Andrea, you petty psycho!!!"],["","Deborah looks on in shock as a familiar face barrels out of the hallway just ahead, several pursuers right on her tail."],["","She has factored in the chance that Bertha is locked up here and has run rescue drills with Verna, but the scene unfolding before her is totally off the charts."],["Deborah","Bertha, come quickly!"],["Bertha","Who! Huh, Deborah!? How did you—"],["Deborah","We'll talk later. Come on!"],["","With no time to question anything, Bertha circles around the container and moves toward Deborah."],["","Deborah tracks the pursuers' positions, hitting the detonator right on cue."],["Muskrat Mercenary","Wh-What?!"],["","Though the small chain reaction packs little punch, it kicks up enough force to blast the stacked crates apart."],["","Caught flat-footed, the Muskrat mercs take the brunt: charges clip some directly, flying crates flatten others, and the concussive blast leaves the rest reeling."],["","Covering her ears against the relentless noise, Bertha rushes over to Deborah and blurts out the question that's been on her mind."],["Bertha","Since when are you running stealth-and-demolition ops...?! Don't tell me you picked that up from the GSA?"],["Deborah","Doesn't matter who I learned it from, as long as it works."],["","Using the chaos as cover, Deborah leads Bertha out of the pursuers' line of sight. But a racket this loud is bound to alert the whole base, and they need to pull off an exit fast."],["Bertha","How do we get out?"],["Deborah","Get on that, break through the wall, and charge straight out!"],["","Following Deborah along the escape route, Bertha only now clocks the cluster of unmanned STs sitting not far off."],["Deborah","They're distracted, so let's \"borrow\" some of their STs!"],["","Meanwhile, the main Muskrat outfit prepping for deployment is thrown into sudden disarray by the surprise blast."],["Muskrat Mercenary Captain","Captain Andrea, Bertha and the intruders have taken our STs—they're running riot in the hangar!"],["Muskrat Mercenary Captain","Shall we recall the squad that just deployed?"],["Andrea","No, the first and second squads will proceed to support Carlo as planned. I'll lead the remaining forces to eliminate the invaders myself."],["","In the pilot cabin, Andrea's hand trembles slightly as she grips the control stick, her heart gradually filling with uncontrollable anger."],["Andrea","...You made the worst choice, Bertha."]],"468377301":[["Bertha","Hah... hah... Seriously, it just never ends..."],["","Bertha pants heavily, struggling to maneuver her increasingly damaged ST. On the other side, Deborah isn't faring much better."],["","Although they've managed to destroy several Muskrat STs and even repelled an attack by Andrea herself, they're ultimately outnumbered and surrounded."],["Bertha","How much ammo do you have left?"],["Deborah","None."],["","With that, Deborah's ST disengages its weapon mount. The machine gun, already empty, slams heavily onto the ground, its barrel still glowing from the sustained fire, now bent from the impact."],["Bertha","What? Doesn't that mean we're doomed?!"],["","Andrea has also noticed that the two are long out of ammunition, and she orders the mercenaries to press forward in groups, tightening the encirclement further and further."],["Deborah","Doomed? On the contrary, we've already bought enough time."],["Deborah","Looks like we win."],["","As soon as Deborah finishes speaking, a sudden rail gun attack pierces through the Muskrat battle line from the side, catching two closely positioned STs off guard and penetrating them directly."],["","Using this as a signal, multiple STs launch an assault on the Muskrat Mercenaries. They're of various types, some bearing the emblem of the Luno Family, some carrying the mark of the Harpy Guild."],["","Leading them at the front is the heavily armored ST Colossus, its rail gun freshly fired."],["Vincenza","Deborah, Bertha, fall back."],["Bertha","Vincenza!? You... when did you get such a cool new ST!? How many Milkhama dollars did it set you back? I want one too—"],["Deborah","Save the window shopping for later—let's move!"],["","Deborah works the controls, shoving Bertha's spellbound ST back behind friendly lines. The Muskrat Mercenaries try to cut them off, only to catch a heavier wall of counter-fire."],["Andrea","New objective: All units, fall back to the bunkers!"],["","To avoid further losses, Andrea has no choice but to abandon the plan to pursue Bertha and Deborah."],["","Her quick read on the field is clear: outgunned and outnumbered, their best bet is to dig into the bunkers and buy some time."],["","Yet five minutes pass, and Vincenza's forces never follow up with a full assault, only probing the base's entrances with intermittent fire."],["Andrea","...Oh no!"],["","Something clicks, and she diverts base power straight into the radar and optical scopes, firing up a high-output rescan of the hostile units nearby."],["","Sure enough, Vincenza's unit—all bluster just a moment ago—drops straight into a retreat after taking in Bertha and the others, leaving only a few tactical STs out on the perimeter to keep up suppressing fire."],["","Tucking themselves into the bunker has cost the Muskrats any chance to chase or reposition—and worse, Vincenza's squad is falling back straight toward Port Kadrey."],["Andrea","Squads one and two, heads up: scrap the rendezvous and hit them now alongside the Carlo Legion—we have to secure that target data!"],["","Realizing Vincenza played her with that tactical feint, Andrea is left pinning her hopes on the forward strike teams and the Carlo Legion."],["Andrea","Let's hope Carlo Kottel actually proves useful for once."],["","Meanwhile, in a study inside a manor just north of downtown Port Kadrey, the former head of the Luno Family, Genovese, sits back in his chair resting his eyes."],["","Ever since signing that deal with the GSA and passing the reins to his daughter, Vincenza, he's enjoyed an easy life he never knew before."],["","On one hand, the severe injuries from that battle still haven't fully healed, and he needs regular rest. On the other, Vincenza has been handling most matters well, leaving him little need to intervene."],["","...That said, he's already aware of the crisis she's facing within the family. But he can't step in—not yet. The new head must put down the internal unrest herself. It's a deadly trial, but an unavoidable one."],["","Just then, the double doors fly open, and a mess of hurried footsteps approaches, stopping right before the desk. Genovese finally opens his eyes, fixing a sharp stare on the two men out front."],["Genovese","Forgot how to knock, Carlo? Garcia?"],["Garcia","Boss Luno..."],["Carlo","Oh, right. My mistake."],["","With a mocking smile, Carlo taps twice on the desk with his knuckles."],["Carlo","Satisfied now, former Boss Genovese?"],["","Genovese doesn't flinch. Instead, he sizes up the others who barged in with them—familiar Family members, rival gang lieutenants he's tangled with before, and Ovett faces he's never seen in his life."],["","At the same time, he notices that the guards at the door have silently fallen into pools of blood, and all the communicators on the table show signs of interference and disconnection."],["Genovese","Recruiting allies, infiltrating the manor, cutting off communications... This doesn't seem like your usual style."],["Carlo","After all, since you're the opponent, I must give it my all."],["","Carlo pulls up a chair and sits down, his expression growing slightly more serious."],["Carlo","Surrender, Genovese. As long as you surrender, those in the family who are watching will also give up their resistance. This way, I won't have to personally send old friends on their way."],["Genovese","Even if I surrender, Vincenza won't let you go."],["Carlo","Vincenza? She's a bright girl, I'll admit it—but ultimately she's just a girl who grew up in an ivory tower."],["Carlo","Take a look at the familiar faces in this room. The bloodbath in the mines twenty-four years ago, the port turf war eighteen years ago, the pushback against Doll five years back, and that death match with the GSA just last month..."],["Carlo","Which one of us didn't claw our way out of hell with you? And Vincenza, what's she got to stand against us? Playing lapdog to the GSA?"],["Carlo","After that explosion in the mines, the GSA can barely look after themselves—even that old hag Rosemary got dragged down with them. Who's left to stand against us?!"],["","As if pouring out the resentment in his heart, Carlo grows more and more agitated as he speaks."],["Carlo","The Luno Family needs to get back where it belongs—just like when we took Kadrey, taking everything we want with blood and oaths, not wagging our tails for a bunch of bullshit bureaucrats!"],["Genovese","Heh... Hahahahaha! What a pathetic sight you are, Carlo."],["","In contrast to the indignant Carlo, Genovese laughs heartily, as if genuinely amused."],["Carlo","...What?"],["Genovese","The Luno Family was never built on blood and oaths. It was built on loyalty and bonds. After all these years... you still don't understand that."],["Genovese","What you're trying to protect isn't the Family's place. It's your own interests in Kadrey: the smuggling, the drugs."],["Carlo","You...!"],["","Carlo slams the desk and stands up, hand diving inside his suit for his gun, but touching something else first brings him right back down."],["Carlo","I know why you believe Vincenza can win. You've been holding something back. But unfortunately..."],["","Seeing the ebony box with the Luno mark appear in Carlo's hand, Genovese's expression finally shifts."],["Genovese","Did you kill Bertha?"],["Carlo","Too bad... no. That jinx doesn't have much skill, but she does get lucky. Either way, whether she lives or dies doesn't matter."],["","Carlo opens the box and takes out a crystal—clear as glass, faintly glowing blue. It's high-purity arashi essence."],["","Only Genovese and Carlo in that room know it holds vital data packed in at extreme density."],["Carlo","The prize behind this \"key\" will be mine to use, not Vincenza's."],["Genovese","...So this is why you didn't kill me the moment you had the chance."],["Genovese","I never thought you'd sink low enough to sell out a secret our own people died to protect in the mines twenty-four years ago."],["Carlo","Leaving it untouched till the GSA takes every last scrap—that's what really spits on their graves!"],["Carlo","Tell me: the things taken from the Obsidian lab during the mine riots twenty-four years ago—where did you hide them?!"],["Genovese","..."],["","Genovese says nothing. He just fixes Carlo with a sharp, icy stare that sends a chill down his spine."],["Carlo","Since you insist on playing the hero, don't blame me for being ruthless!"],["","At his nod, one of his men steps up carrying a device, its bizarre shape setting off Genovese's instincts immediately."],["Garcia","Carlo, wait! That device will tear him apart—are you really about to use that on Genovese?!"],["Carlo","Had he cooperated, I wouldn't be using a toy like this—but now..."],["","Several of Carlo's subordinates restrain Genovese as Carlo picks up the device."],["Carlo","You brought this on yourself, Genovese Luno!"]],"468381101":[["","In the early morning, the citizens of Kadrey are awakened by a series of explosions."],["","Carlo's coalition slips across Kadrey well ahead of time, quickly locking down the Luno estate while hitting anyone refusing to back him."],["","The family capos backing Vincenza, the cops and soldiers that wouldn't take bribes, rival gangs trying to play both sides—every last one gets hit without mercy."],["UNCS 1st Lieutenant","6th Squad, signal lost... Damn it, they couldn't break through either!?"],["UNCS Soldier","Captain, the enemy is advancing! We can't hold them off!"],["","The NDF garrison stationed in Kadrey is small, but made up of elite troops. Even ambushed by a force far larger than their own, they still mount a coordinated counterattack, but that resistance is now on the verge of collapse."],["","Watching his unit's STs torn apart one by one and losing contact with soldier after soldier, Lieutenant Angelo, commander of the NDF garrison, stares with bloodshot eyes, every order he barks tearing out of his throat like a roar crossed with a sob."],["","BOOM! Another NDF ST crashes down under the siege of the Carlo Legion. Lieutenant Angelo feels the last string in his mind snap completely."],["UNCS 1st Lieutenant","Everyone fall back to the base, now!!"],["","Ordering his men to fall back, he drives his ST straight toward the perimeter."],["UNCS Soldier","Captain!?"],["UNCS 1st Lieutenant","Don't worry about me! Retreat to the base—that's an order!!"],["","Pushing his ST's engine to maximum output, Lieutenant Angelo rams the nearest member of Carlo's forces at terrifying speed, the drive wheels on the machine's feet kicking up showers of sparks against the ground."],["","Caught off guard, the enemy machine spins out of balance before a point-blank shotgun blast tears straight through the pilot's cabin."],["","After destroying the enemy ST, he holds onto the wreck, plowing forward and using it as a shield against bursts of machine-gun fire until he reaches the cover of a nearby building."],["","His move pulls the attention of every enemy machine on the field, and the shift in their battle lines reveals a key target—a Euclase ST riding the front line, directing the assault."],["","That is undoubtedly the enemy's commander."],["UNCS 1st Lieutenant","...Take him down!"],["","Before the enemy can finish regrouping, Lieutenant Angelo decisively drives his ST straight at the Euclase, unloading the last of his remaining firepower."],["","Maybe caught off guard, maybe just arrogant, the targeted commander holds his ground, evasively cutting left and right to dodge the fire, which lets Angelo close the gap straight into melee range."],["UNCS 1st Lieutenant","You're mine!"],["","Ignoring the gunfire pouring in from all sides, he lines up the commander's machine, ready to ram it and pull off the exact same move—"],["","The next second, the display before his eyes abruptly tilts. The charging ST loses its balance, barely clipping the commander's machine before spinning off course and crashing to the ground a short distance away."],["UNCS 1st Lieutenant","What...?"],["","Only then does he realize both legs of his ST have been sliced clean off, while the Euclase stands holding a pair of blades."],["ST System","Warning: The power module is severely damaged. Please withdraw from combat immediately."],["","Immobilized, Lieutenant Angelo knows his last-ditch gamble has completely failed."],["UNCS 1st Lieutenant","Who the hell are you!?"],["","Surprisingly, the other side doesn't cut the line. Yet the moment the face appears in the feed, Lieutenant Angelo reels."],["UNCS 1st Lieutenant","Why is it you... Genovese Luno!?"],["Genovese","..."],["","Not a trace of emotion shows on his face. Genovese merely maneuvers his ST, reorganizing the front line to resume the assault on the NDF camp."],["UNCS 1st Lieutenant","Why are you helping Carlo hit Kadrey!?"],["","As if mocking the unanswered demand, a nearby member of Carlo's forces levels a machine gun at him, finger tightening on the trigger—"],["Gregory","Know when to call it quits, kid."],["","With that sudden voice breaking across the comms, Carlo's forces look up to find unknown STs swarming in from all directions, opening fire on their lines."],["Gregory","Doug, get that NDF guy somewhere safe, then transmit the signal as planned."],["Doug","Got it! But boss, is that really Genovese in that Euclase?"],["Gregory","No mistake. Carlo pulled out that \"device\"... Now we owe the Luno Family big time."],["","Watching Carlo's outfit quickly rally a counteroffensive under Genovese's command, Gregory winces with a rising headache."],["Gregory","Alright, push it—give me everything you've got! We hold them here. No one lets that leader slip out, got it?"],["Gregory","The rest... depends on how fast our allies move."],["","Around fifteen minutes later, Vincenza finally arrives in Kadrey with her unit."],["Bertha","Is this really Kadrey?"],["","The flashes of gunfire take the place of a sun that hasn't yet fully risen, casting the entire city in a burning red glow. Everywhere, ST units clash in open combat, while gang fighters wage brutal street battles through the alleys."],["","This isn't some turf war anymore; it's a full-blown local conflict, far outstripping the old clashes between the Luno Family and the GSA."],["Gregory","Took you long enough... cough, cough."],["Deborah","Gregory, how are you holding up?"],["Gregory","Hanging on, but not for long... Miss Vincenza, your old man really is something else."],["Vincenza","What?"],["Gregory","Look for yourself. I need to save my breath—Doug, drop the right flank! Let them push in before opening up!"],["","Without the leeway for a full debrief, Gregory manages his outnumbered squad while piping his combat feeds and intel over to Vincenza's channel."],["","Carlo's force stormed the Luno estate, hit the NDF and rival gangs next, and is now locked in a brutal stalemate with the Harpy Guild..."],["","And every scrap of intel points to one unthinkable reality: the man leading Carlo's forces from the front is Genovese."],["Vincenza","Father...? Why would he..."],["","Even Vincenza can't help but feel a bit shaken. She repeatedly checks the intel, trying to find evidence to refute it."],["Bertha","Hey, Harpy—are you sure about this? How the hell would the Luno boss be backing Carlo?!"],["Gregory","It isn't by his own will."],["Gregory","The \"Alpha-Type Hyper-Aptamer Research Device\"—Carlo Kottel is using it to control Genovese Luno, putting him out front to lead the troops and draw all the fire!"],["Gregory","Just like what Blair did to those test-subject units in the NDF."],["Vincenza","Hyper-Aptamer!? Why would Carlo have such a thing—"],["","After teaming up with the GSA, Vincenza learned through various channels about this special tech hailed as the NDF's ace in the hole, even tracking down escaped NDF deserters on the GSA's dime."],["","She knows how strictly the NDF controls anything tied to that technology. If it had leaked from within their ranks straight to Carlo, the GSA wouldn't be completely in the dark, unless—"],["","Her pulse hammers with raw anxiety, but her mind races ahead, cold and sharp."],["Vincenza","Unless it was obtained through means that even the GSA cannot control..."],["","That's when the truth she's been kept from snaps into focus."],["Vincenza","It was Harpy...! Carlo didn't just hit Harpy's depot for guns! Gregory, you've been lying to us this whole time!"],["Gregory","...Sorry, Miss Vincenza. Harpy put me on this under the table specifically so word wouldn't get out."],["Gregory","Guess there's no point hiding it now... You called it. Carlo and the Muskrat Mercenaries looted that forbidden piece of tech straight out of Harpy's stockpile."],["Deborah","Wait, how did Harpy even get their hands on something like that?"],["Gregory","West Milkhama is crawling with Obsidian and NDF research labs. Blair gave the order to torch everything before he fell, but he didn't have enough boots on the ground to wipe the slate clean."],["Gregory","In the chaos of the evacuation, a chunk of the gear, the data, and even the staff slipped out from under the factions' thumbs, winding up in the pockets of gray-market outfits like Vesper and Harpy."],["Gregory","This \"Alpha-Type Hyper-Aptamer Research Device\" was originally meant to be shipped to headquarters for study—but it was stolen the night before transfer. Worse still, the Ovett Revolutionary Army knows how to use it."],["","By now, Vincenza has pieced the whole picture together. She calms down fast, her mind already shifting to counters."],["","She doesn't just need to wipe out every hostile tearing through Kadrey; she has to bring Genovese out in one piece. Both hinge on the exact same move."],["Vincenza","No matter what, we must stop my father first."],["Bertha","Hold on, Vincenza, you're actually taking a shot at Boss Luno!?"],["Vincenza","We're not destroying the unit. We cut its drive systems, then find a way to shut the device down..."],["Natalia","Smart call, but you're missing a critical step—keep cockpit aux power alive for a beat to let Genovese lose consciousness before you pull the plug on the device."],["Natalia","That's the only way to keep his brainwaves from flatlining or spiking out of control."],["","The voice patching in out of nowhere catches everyone flat-footed."],["Deborah","Natalia Coronado... After all this, the GSA finally decides to show their face?"],["Natalia","Why would we step into the mud if our partners can handle things smoothly?"],["","Natalia keeps smiling, though the words dripping from her lips are pure acid. Vincenza doesn't flinch, meeting her blow for blow."],["Vincenza","Maybe this mess would've been handled smoothly if your people had caught wind of the Hyper-Aptamer device in time..."],["Vincenza","You're dragging your feet on sending troops because your own hands are tied... What you should be doing right now is backing us up, not testing our nerves."],["Natalia","I won't bother denying your little assumptions, Vincenza Luno, but get one thing straight—the GSA never plays its last hand."],["Natalia","We aren't the ones desperate for a lifeline right now. The Luno Family is... and that's exactly what I'm offering you."],["","The second she finishes speaking, a data packet punches straight through the comms firewall and force-loads into Vincenza's ST OS: a real-time signal map tracking every NDF machine active across Kadrey."],["Natalia","My strike team has already reached Kadrey to support the NDF counteroffensive. If all goes well, they may be able to help you safely remove the Hyper-Aptamer device."],["Natalia","Provided, of course, you clean up this mess within thirty minutes."],["","The smirk plastered across Natalia's face makes Deborah bristle with disgust, while Bertha pulls a face beside her."],["","Vincenza takes a long, slow breath, locking her focus in cold and sharp."],["Vincenza","I'll have Kadrey locked down in twenty minutes."],["Natalia","Oh?"],["Vincenza","On one condition—your people and the NDF fall under my command."],["Vincenza","We shatter their lines in one push before they can even react."]],"468381301":[["","In the gardens of the Luno estate north of Kadrey, a massive crater tears through the ground, laying bare an underground steel corridor below."],["","Flanked by his thugs, a man in a sharp suit and dark sunglasses walks through the long-abandoned passage—Carlo and Garcia's crew."],["","Using the Alpha-Type Hyper-Aptamer Research Device, they ripped the warehouse's coordinates right out of Genovese... Nobody would have guessed it sat buried beneath ground they walked over every single day."],["","Carlo edges closer to the prize he's craved for so long, but victory tastes entirely sour."],["Carlo","Useless bastards, the whole lot of them!! You can't even hold the line for half an hour!?"],["","Shocked and furious after getting word that the front is caving in, Carlo takes a ten-second call before violently hurling his phone against the wall, smashing it to pieces."],["Garcia","The device signal is dropping. Hard to believe Vincenza's crew actually pinned down Genovese."],["Carlo","...It's not over. None of this is over!"],["","Carlo pulls out a control console with an antenna."],["Garcia","A remote detonator? Wait, Carlo, what are you doing!?"],["Carlo","Genovese lost. He's completely useless now."],["Carlo","While those idiots are busy trying to take off the Hyper-Aptamer device, the bomb I rigged on him will blow them all straight to hell!"],["Garcia","You rigged a bomb on Genovese's ST? You sick bastard, why the hell would you do that!?"],["Garcia","Once we take the Luno stash, we've already won! There's no reason to kill him—"],["Carlo","We let him walk, and you think he lets us walk too!? Snap out of your fantasy, Garcia!"],["Carlo","To the Luno Family, we're dirty traitors, through and through! At this point, it's us or them!"],["Carlo","Remember, the second you joined my crew, there was no turning back!"],["Garcia","I...!"],["","Garcia wants to snap back, but no words come. Just like Carlo says, he has to ride this road to the bitter end."],["","Seeing Garcia's reaching hand drop limp, Carlo sneers, flips the safety latch, and drives his thumb down toward the detonator."],["Garcia","Stop—!"],["","Everything goes black before Garcia's eyes."],["","\"Here before my brothers and sisters, sealed in blood, I take this eternal oath. Loyalty, honor, silence, the three vows etched upon my heart...\""],["","\"By blood I swear to uphold the glory and laws of the family, yielding unconditional obedience to our leader's word...\""],["","\"Should I stray and betray the trust placed in me, I welcome the family's judgment, praying it cuts worse than death...\""],["","\"May my loyalty stand firm as stone, my will unbending as steel...\""],["",".............................."],["Genovese","On your feet, Garcia. I don't need anyone to kneel before me, I only need loyalty."],["Garcia","...!"],["Garcia","Boss Luno—!"],["","BANG—!"],["","The finger already brushing against the trigger loses all its strength at the sudden crack of gunfire."],["","A clean hole punches straight between Carlo's brows, dark crimson welling out... The manic sneer on his face freezes in place forever."],["","Everyone freezes, staring in pure disbelief at the pistol smoking in Garcia's hand—Garcia included."],["","Shock, terror, fury, relief—a storm of emotion hits him all at once, leaving behind an unprecedented, weightless calm."],["","Seconds drag by before anyone snaps out of it."],["Carlo Legion Officer","Carlo!!"],["","Carlo's lieutenant screams, ripping out his sidearm and firing wild rounds at Garcia, who still stands rooted to the spot, before lunging toward Carlo's body."],["","Blind rage ruins the lieutenant's aim, but two rounds still tear into Garcia's torso."],["Garcia","Ugh...!"],["","The strong impact and intense pain make him stagger a few steps, lose his balance, and fall to the ground."],["","Seeing this, the other members of the Carlo Legion also draw their weapons and surround him."],["Carlo Legion Officer","Kill him! Kill him! Avenge our boss!!!"],["Bertha","Don't even think about it!"],["","Right then, a hail of gunfire erupts from the dark, tearing clean through Carlo's unprepared thugs."],["Carlo Legion Officer","E-Enemies! Return fire—gah!?"],["","Before the lieutenant can shout an order, a round from another angle drops him where he stands. The ebony box he just pulled off Carlo's corpse is caught securely in the attacker's grip."],["Deborah","Hmph, you rats are all the same. You're not worthy of holding this."],["","With the initiative on their side, Bertha and Deborah unleash a barrage of fire, cutting down what's left of the Carlo Legion."],["Garcia","Hahaha..."],["","Blood pools steadily beneath Garcia's gut, yet a dry laugh rattles out of his throat as he lies on the floor... He knows the uprising is over."],["","Light, measured footsteps approach from behind. Garcia can't see the face, but he knows exactly who it is."],["Garcia","Keep moving forward... Vincenza..."],["Garcia","The Muskrat Mercenaries... those Ovett bastards... don't let them... get ahead..."],["Vincenza","...I know."],["","She doesn't stop, offering only that brief reply as she walks past him. Through his blurring eyes, Garcia can't make out her expression."],["Vincenza","Bertha, wait here for Gregory. Bring Garcia back with him."],["Garcia","Don't... worry about me..."],["Vincenza","That's the boss's call. You don't get a say."],["Garcia","..."],["","From start to finish, Vincenza doesn't look at Garcia once."],["Vincenza","The rest of you, push forward with me... Let's put an end to this farce."],["Ovett Revolutionary Army","The Carlo Legion is done for."],["","The secret vault Genovese Luno spent years carving out is now completely locked down by Ovett's Revolutionary Army."],["","If Carlo's crew were still around, they'd be floored—because the boots on the ground don't just belong to the Muskrat Mercenaries, but to dozens of fresh faces they've never laid eyes on."],["Liliya","Is that so? Even more useless than expected... Andrea really should choose her partners more carefully."],["Liliya","Fortunately, we didn't make the trip for nothing."],["","The vault is packed with ST frames, arashi matter, and other high-grade prizes—spoils of war hauled out by the mining gangs active over twenty years ago, before the Milkhama War reached a fever pitch."],["","After Genovese Luno became the sole boss of that era and land, these things became his assets... and the only basis for commemorating those comrades lost in the war."],["","Liliya has learned all this from the intel Andrea provided, but she has no interest in it whatsoever."],["","All she cares about is the small chip in her hand."],["Liliya","Francis Gideon's technical notes were actually here all along."],["Liliya","They say the attack on the Obsidian Institute all those years ago was deliberately orchestrated by certain major powers... but now, it seems that wasn't the whole story."],["","Otherwise, how could something this important have remained hidden for so long in the private vault of a criminal family?"],["","Liliya has no interest in digging up the buried truths of the past. Right now, all she cares about is decoding the chip—and studying the invaluable data left behind by the creator of the legendary arashium technology."],["","Bang! Bang! Sudden bursts of gunfire tear through the entrance, cutting down the Ovett soldiers where they stand. Almost instinctively, the others dive for cover, weapons raised as they assess the situation."],["Ovett Revolutionary Army","It's Vincenza Luno! They're here!"],["Liliya","They're moving faster than expected... Looks like it's time to go."],["","Liliya carefully places the chip inside a sealed container, then calmly orders the Ovett Revolutionary Army to fall back to the designated extraction point."],["","The pursuing Luno forces seem to realize what they are planning. They alternate between firing and advancing, steadily trying to close the distance. But the well-trained Ovett forces respond immediately, holding them at bay and denying them any chance to press closer."],["","Just as Liliya and her team reach the extraction point and prepare to board their STs, the ambushers already lying in wait seize their chance."],["Vincenza","Open fire."],["Deborah","Have a taste of this!"],["","At Vincenza's command, a hail of Gatling fire tears toward Liliya's exposed back."],["Ovett Revolutionary Army","Not a chance!"],["","Several soldiers from the Ovett Revolutionary Army rearguard move without hesitation, deliberately throwing themselves into the line of fire to shield Liliya."],["","One falls. Then another. Then a third... In barely five seconds, four Ovett soldiers are torn apart by the barrage."],["","But those few seconds are enough for Liliya and the others to board their STs."],["Vincenza","Fall back! Abandon the pursuit!"],["","Vincenza gives the order just in time. As the Luno forces begin to withdraw, a grenade lands exactly where they were about to advance. The violent blast sends the pursuers sprawling and brings the passage crashing down."],["Deborah","These Ovettians are completely insane!"],["Vincenza","The GSA and Harpy ST units are already on the ground. Let them deal with the Ovett Revolutionary Army."],["","They turn toward the storage room on the other side. Its door still hangs open, revealing the valuables and assorted junk piled within."],["Deborah","What do you plan to do with all this?"],["Vincenza","...We don't have a better option, Deborah."],["","Vincenza, who rarely shows weakness, lets out a quiet sigh."],["Vincenza","Whatever Father's reasons were for preserving these secrets..."],["Vincenza","If the Luno Family is going to have a future, we have no choice but to put them on the table."],["","One day later, in Kadrey City..."],["","Heavy equipment is everywhere across the city, hauling off wrecked ST frames and collapsed rubble, while cleanup crews work the streets, erasing the scars of urban combat."],["","Even the hospitals are overflowing. Luckily, the UNCS government has dispatched field medical units in time, pitching field tents and requisitioning commercial towers to handle the crushing wave of casualties."],["","...Even though the battle is over, the wounds of Kadrey City are still bleeding, and even when they heal, the scar will remain for a long time."],["Vincenza","......"],["","Vincenza Luno stands quietly by the street, gazing at the hometown she fought hard to reclaim but couldn't fully protect."],["","Beep—suddenly, her phone emits an alert."],["Vincenza","Deborah, how are things?"],["Deborah","Just wrapped up the check. Winston... the scientist the GSA sent over, he managed to dismantle the alpha device. Genovese is still under, but his vitals have stabilized."],["Vincenza","Is that so...? Great..."],["","The stone crushing Vincenza's chest finally shifts and drops, though it hasn't completely hit the floor."],["Vincenza","And what about Garcia?"],["Deborah","...He's not looking good."],["Deborah","Although the bullet that hit the abdomen miraculously avoided the aorta, it still tore a hole in the intestines."],["Deborah","The doctor worked all night, and now the internal bleeding has mostly stopped, but the wound's infection has already spread... Whether he can pull through, no one knows."],["Vincenza","...Have the doctors save him. Whatever it takes."],["","As she speaks, a black sedan swings around the corner and glides to a stop in front of her."],["","The door clicks open, and a GSA agent steps out."],["UNCS Agent","Sorry to keep you waiting, Miss Vincenza. Please, get in."],["","Overhearing the noise through the receiver, Deborah's low voice turns even more anxious."],["Deborah","...Are you really going through with this, Vincenza?"],["Deborah","A \"joint conference between the GSA, Doll, Harpy, and Luno\"... Sounds pretty on paper, but it looks like a kangaroo court set up to hang the family out to dry."],["Vincenza","Maybe, but they aren't working as a single front... This meeting is more like a poker table."],["Vincenza","If they want to squeeze real profit out of this game, they won't cut the Luno Family loose. Play the chips right, and our rivals' friends can easily become ours."],["Vincenza","...The Luno Family isn't going down like this. I promise you."],["","This is a promise to Deborah, and to herself."],["","Putting aside her doubts and concerns, Vincenza strides toward the GSA sedan."]]};
